[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"639","stub":{"id":"639","section":"5. Skookum Canyon: Turner Creek to Packsaddle","altname":"Skookum Canyon","river":"St. Joe","difficulty":"IIIplus","states":["USA-IDA"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"migration-runnable","latestReading":{"value":"5150","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":"The Turner Flat Campground (Highway 50 mile 55.9) features 10 camp units, 1 group camping area to accommodate up to 15 people, potable water (June-October), and vault toilets. Sites 2, 3, and 4 are interconnected and include the group camping area with a field that has a few tent sites for a group. The rest of the campsites are in the forest. River access for rafts or kayaks is easy here. If the campground is full, kayakers can access the river near the upstream exit of the campground at the Trail 17 bridge (Highway 50 mile 56.4).","id":"110765","location":{"latitude":"47.236873","longitude":"-115.656247"},"name":"Turner Flat Campground, Put-In","distance":"0","photoID":"lwwIvUId5JlM7yrWKYQqw","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"The entrance to Skookum Canyon is marked by an obvious horizon line (visible from Highway 50 mile 53.6). The most significant drops come at the start and then the action gradually tapers off over the next mile.","id":"OB1eUPyy0xISmm1DDXY15","location":{"latitude":"47.229191","longitude":"-115.694376"},"name":"Skookum Canyon Entrance","distance":"2.38","difficulty":"III","approximate":false,"photoID":"eotIXiEmAobqwRoMyhyob"},{"type":"access","description":"The end of the whitewater is marked by a cableway that crosses the river. A pull out here at Highway 50 mile 52.5 serves as an alternate take-out for kayakers who don't want to paddle the remaining flatwater down to the campground. It does require a short climb up the bank to the highway.","id":"jV9zA1D0iEe6YK9EVOhNT","location":{"latitude":"47.228287","longitude":"-115.71093"},"name":"Cableway Access","distance":"3.48","photoID":"cmYwAvFKIpCjreuFaoWKF","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":"Located at Highway 50 Mile 51.4. This Forest Service campground offers two camp sites, a vault toilet, drinking water (June- October), and a dedicated boat launch area immediately downstream of the first campsite. Parking is available on a pullout along the highway at the upstream exit of the camgpround near the toilet.","id":"116034","location":{"latitude":"47.231699","longitude":"-115.730748"},"name":"Packsaddle Campground, Take-Out","distance":"4.36","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"D9JRNeBCZvj2ViRfqhyi1","ext":"jpg","post_id":"K9cnuTI4ltrTgt1bsuVU0","description":"","caption":"Skookum Canyon","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Thomas O'Keefe and Rie Yamazaki","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2021-07-02T03:35:12.000Z","updated_at":"2023-02-10T03:35:12.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/D9JRNeBCZvj2ViRfqhyi1","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/D9JRNeBCZvj2ViRfqhyi1"}},{"id":"eotIXiEmAobqwRoMyhyob","ext":"jpg","post_id":"K9cnuTI4ltrTgt1bsuVU0","description":"","caption":"Skookum Canyon","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Thomas O'Keefe and Rie Yamazaki","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2021-07-02T03:35:12.000Z","updated_at":"2023-02-10T03:35:12.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/eotIXiEmAobqwRoMyhyob","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/eotIXiEmAobqwRoMyhyob"}},{"id":"tD1AOe42sKzlMREUKn2Dh","ext":"jpg","post_id":"K9cnuTI4ltrTgt1bsuVU0","description":"","caption":"Entering Skookum Canyon","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Thomas O'Keefe and Rie Yamazaki","poi_id":"OB1eUPyy0xISmm1DDXY15","photo_date":"2021-07-02T03:35:12.000Z","updated_at":"2023-02-10T03:35:12.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/tD1AOe42sKzlMREUKn2Dh","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/tD1AOe42sKzlMREUKn2Dh"}},{"id":"cmYwAvFKIpCjreuFaoWKF","ext":"jpg","post_id":"K9cnuTI4ltrTgt1bsuVU0","description":"","caption":"Cableway Access","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Thomas O'Keefe and Rie Yamazaki","poi_id":"jV9zA1D0iEe6YK9EVOhNT","photo_date":"2021-07-02T03:35:12.000Z","updated_at":"2023-02-10T03:35:12.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/cmYwAvFKIpCjreuFaoWKF","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/cmYwAvFKIpCjreuFaoWKF"}},{"id":"uMuFVnUp29mFouNuD3SG5","ext":"jpg","post_id":"K9cnuTI4ltrTgt1bsuVU0","description":"An inviting side canyon towards the end of Skookum Canyon.","caption":"Sisters Creek Side Canyon","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Thomas O'Keefe and Rie Yamazaki","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2021-07-02T03:35:12.000Z","updated_at":"2023-02-10T03:35:12.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/uMuFVnUp29mFouNuD3SG5","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/uMuFVnUp29mFouNuD3SG5"}},{"id":"lwwIvUId5JlM7yrWKYQqw","ext":"jpg","post_id":"K9cnuTI4ltrTgt1bsuVU0","description":"Turner Flat Campground is a good place to camp and stage trips for those enjoying runs through Skookum Canyon.","caption":"Turner Flat Campground","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Thomas O'Keefe and Rie Yamazaki","poi_id":"110765","photo_date":"2021-07-02T03:35:12.000Z","updated_at":"2023-02-10T03:35:12.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/lwwIvUId5JlM7yrWKYQqw","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/lwwIvUId5JlM7yrWKYQqw"}}],"detail":{"id":"639","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"The run begins from Bird Creek Boat Launch or Turner Flat Campground and the first two miles are relatively flat with occassional riffles. Once you reach the obvious horizon line marking the entrance to Skookum Canyon the action begins. The two most significant drops are at the start but the action continues for the next mile down to Sisters Creek, an intriguing tributary that enters from river left and a side canyon that invites exploration. While this run is short, it is a fun hour long adventure when you are looking for a quick hit with easy logistics. Highway 50, a paved two-lane road parallels the entire run although the guardrail partially obscures the view into Skookum Canyon. At low flows this river becomes more class II.","averageGradient":null,"maxGradient":null,"length":"4.6","correlations":[{"reachID":"639","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"500","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"25000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"ST JOE RIVER AT CALDER, ID","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"12414500","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"5150","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"9.02","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"47.2744444","longitude":"-116.1888889"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/12414500","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/12414500/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":null,"comment":null,"status":{"status":"migration-runnable","latestReading":{"value":"5150","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null}}],"pointOfInterestIDs":["110765","OB1eUPyy0xISmm1DDX